      en: "The Bezisten in Yambol is one of the best-preserved monuments of Ottoman civil architecture on the Balkan Peninsula. Built around 1509 during the reign of Sultan Bayezid II, the building served for centuries as a covered market for valuable goods such as fabrics, spices, and precious metals. The architecture is defined by massive stone walls and an impressive arrangement of domes, which provide the interior with unique acoustics and atmosphere. Following a comprehensive restoration in 2015, the Bezisten was transformed into a modern interactive museum that presents the history of the Yambol region using holograms, 3D projections, and audiovisual effects. Today, the building functions not only as a historical monument but also as a vibrant cultural center, hosting concerts, exhibitions, and public events in a truly unique historical setting.",
